            <ArticleTitle>Pediatric chronic pain: there is hope.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>48-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic pain is prevalent in children and can limit their ability to attend school, socialize with peers, and participate in physical activity. This article describes the advantages of using a multidisciplinary approach to evaluating and treating children with chronic pain and discusses medications and techniques for managing pain and restoring functionality.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
